                <pb facs="0352" n="250" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg250"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 16387/1.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Morgan.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-11-07"><hi rendition="#italic">November 7,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Root instructs Mr. Morgan to convey to the family of the late Don Tomas
                    Estrada Palma an expression of deep sorrow and sympathy in their bereavement.
                    Mr. Root states that he mourns the death of Don Tomas Estrada Palma as the loss
                    of a personal friend as well as a noble pure minded lover of his country.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
